---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

import Collection from "../components/Collection.astro";
import RootLayout from "../layouts/RootLayout.astro";
import PageWithSideBarNav from "@/layouts/PageWithSideBarNav.astro";
const pageTitle = "Federal Agency Links";

// TODO: get posts for each question on this page
const posts = await getCollection("programPost", ({ data }) => {
  return data.programArea === "Acquisition";
});
---

<RootLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <PageWithSideBarNav>
    <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
    <div class="usa-prose">
      <p>
        The Federal Agency Links page provides links to the Environmental Home
        Pages of various Federal agencies. <a
          href="/programs/compliance/stateprograms/"
          target="new">Click here</a
        > to access environmental home pages for all 50 U.S. states.
        <!-- TODO: Add a link here -->
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="">
      <ul class="usa-list">
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.afcec.af.mil/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            Air Force Civil Engineer Center</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The Air Force Civil Engineer Center provides Air Force leaders with
            the comprehensive expertise and professional services necessary to
            protect, preserve, restore, develop and sustain the nation's
            environmental and installation resources.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.safie.hq.af.mil/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            Air Force Installations, Environment and Energy</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            Office of the Assistant Secretary of the Air Force's home page for
            installations, environment, and energy.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.usace.army.mil/Missions/Environmental/Regional-Environmental-and-Energy-Offices-REEOs.aspx"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            Army Regional Environmental and Energy Offices</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The Army Regional Environmental and Energy Offices protect and
            advance Army (and DoD) military readiness by engaging State
            governments, regional Federal agencies and non-governmental
            organizations to promote sustainable installation operations. The
            Army has four Regional Environmental and Energy Offices (REEOs); the
            Northern Office at Aberdeen Proving Ground, Southern Office in
            Atlanta, Central Office in Kansas City, and Western Office in
            Denver. Army is the lead DoD REC for USEPA Region 5 (Northern
            Office), Region 4 (Southern Office), Region 7 (Central Office), and
            Region 8 (Western Office).
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.epa.gov/indoor-air-quality-iaq/federal-interagency-committee-indoor-air-quality"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            CIAQ - Federal Interagency Committee on Indoor Air Quality</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            Charged by Congress (1983) with coordinating public/private research
            on indoor air quality; 24 member agencies. Public webinars/meetings
            with presentations and member agency updates in February, June and
            October. Email: CIAQ@epa.gov , Listserve:
            ciaq-subscribe@lists.epa.gov.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.denix.osd.mil"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            Defense Environmental Network &amp; Information eXchange (DENIX)</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            DENIX is the central platform and information clearinghouse for
            environment, safety and occupational health (ESOH) news,
            information, policy, and guidance. Serving the worldwide greater
            Department of Defense (DoD) community, DENIX offers ESOH
            professionals a vast document library, a gateway to web-based
            environmental compliance tools, an interactive workgroup
            environment, a variety of groupware tools and an active membership
            community numbering thousands.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.denix.osd.mil/nr/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            Department of Defense (DoD) Natural Resources Program</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The DoD Natural Resources Program (NR Program) supports the
            military's testing and training mission by protecting its biological
            resources. The NR Program provides policy, guidance, and oversight
            for management of natural resources on approximately 27 million
            acres of military land, air, and water resources owned or operated
            by DoD. The NR Program's goal is to support the military's combat
            readiness mission by ensuring continued access to realistic habitat
            conditions, while simultaneously working to ensure the long-term
            sustainability of our nation's priceless natural heritage.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.justice.gov/ej/index.html"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            Department of Justice Environmental Programs</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The intent of these pages is to facilitate and communicate DOJ's
            commitment to serving as an example in the area of environmental
            stewardship and compliance with environmental legislation and
            Executive Orders.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.epa.gov/fgc" class="usa-link usa-link--external">
            Federal Green Challenge Website</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The Federal Green Challenge (FGC) is a national effort under EPA's
            Sustainable Materials Management Program, challenging EPA and other
            federal agencies throughout the country to lead by example in
            reducing the federal government's environmental impact. It furthers
            the goals of the President's Executive Order Regarding Efficient
            Federal Operations. This website provides federal installations
            guidance on reducing, reusing, and recycling resources.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.gsa.gov/enviroprograms"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            GSA's Public Building Service Environmental Program</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The Public Buildings Service's environmental goal is to eliminate
            all damage to the environment resulting from its operations. The PBS
            Environment Program works in coordination with the Sustainable
            Design and Energy programs to ensure that PBS continuously makes
            progress towards that goal.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.irs.gov/irm/part1/irm_01-014-012.html"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            Internal Revenue Service (IRS) Environmental Program</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The IRS environmental home page. Provides links to information on
            program elements, roles and responsibilities, training, inspections,
            audits, and assessments.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.nasa.gov/offices/emd/home/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            NASA's Environmental Management Division</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            NASA's Environmental Management Division serves as Agency lead in
            assuring that NASA meets its Federal stewardship responsibilities
            and achieves sustainability while carrying out its primary mission
            of understanding and protecting our home planet, exploring the
            Universe and searching for life, and inspiring the next generation
            of explorers.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.sustainability.gov"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            Office of Federal Sustainability (OFS)</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            Promoting sustainable environmental stewardship throughout the
            federal government.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://eko.usace.army.mil/usacecop/pub/ecop/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            U.S. Army Corps of Engineers' Environmental Community of Practice</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            The Environmental Community of Practice (eCoP) provides the public
            with a central point to access information on all the U.S. Army
            Corps of Engineers environmental programs. The Corps supports or
            manages numerous environmental initiatives including Ecosystem
            Restoration, Formerly Used Defense Sites, Environmental Stewardship,
            support to EPA Superfund and Brownfields programs, Abandoned Mine
            Lands, Formerly Utilized Sites Remedial Action Program, Base
            Realignment and Closure 2005, and Regulatory. The Corps'
            environmental programs support the warfighter and military
            installations worldwide as well as the Corps' public recreation
            facilities throughout the country.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www.aec.army.mil/"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            U.S. Army Environmental Command</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            USAEC is the Army's point organization for implementing
            environmental programs that enhance Army training and operations
            while protecting the environment. As a field-operating agency of the
            ACSIM, USAEC's mission implements the environmental program for the
            Army by providing a broad range of innovative and cost-effective
            products and services in support of Army training, operations, and
            sound stewardship.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="http://www2.epa.gov/enforcement"
            class="usa-link usa-link--external"
          >
            US EPA - Office of Enforcement and Compliance Assurance (OECA)</a
          >

          <p class="margin-top-0">
            Responsible for ensuring the compliance of the regulated community
            with federal environmental statutes.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </PageWithSideBarNav>
</RootLayout>
